{"cuisine/georgian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/georgian-cuisine","n":"Georgian cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Caucasian cuisine","cuisine/caucasian-cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Georgia","intro":[["Georgian cuisine consists of cooking traditions, techniques, and practices of Georgia. Georgian cuisine has a distinct character, while bearing some similarities with various national cuisines of the Caucasus, the Middle East and Eastern Europe. Every region of Georgia has its own distinct style of food preparation. Eating and drinking are important parts of Georgian culture."],["Georgia was one of the countries on the Silk Road, which resulted in travelers influencing Georgian cuisine. The Georgian love of family and friends is one of the reasons why the supra (feast) is so important in Georgia. Supra is offered spontaneously to relatives, friends or guests. Every supra has its tamada (toastmaster), who gives the toast and entertains the guests."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"georgian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":29,"links":[["Achma","dish/achma"],["Ajika","dish/ajika"],["Akhasheni","dish/akhasheni"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chakapuli","dish/chakapuli"],["Chakhokhbili","dish/chakhokhbili"],["Chashushuli","dish/chashushuli"],["Chicken tabaka","dish/chicken-tabaka"],["Churchkhela","dish/churchkhela"],["Dambalkhacho","dish/dambalkhacho"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["Gozinaki","dish/gozinaki"],["Khachapuri","dish/khachapuri"],["Kharcho","dish/kharcho"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Khvanchkara","dish/khvanchkara"],["Kindzmarauli","dish/kindzmarauli"],["Kubdari","dish/kubdari"],["Kuchmachi","dish/kuchmachi"],["Kvass","dish/kvass"],["Lobiani","dish/lobiani"],["Mchadi","dish/mchadi"],["Mujuretuli","dish/mujuretuli"],["Nadugi","dish/nadugi"],["Nigvziani badrijani","dish/nigvziani-badrijani"],["Pkhali","dish/pkhali"],["Shkmeruli","dish/shkmeruli"],["Tsolikouri","dish/tsolikouri"],["Tvishi (wine)","dish/tvishi-wine"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Georgian Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"georgianrecipes.net","note":"Recipe site dedicated to traditional Georgian dishes.","url":"https://georgianrecipes.net/about-georgian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":3,"rows":[{"name":"The Georgian Feast","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Darra Goldstein, 1993","note":"Classic English-language study of Georgian food and culture, with recipes.","url":"https://ucpress.edu/books/the-georgian-feast/paper","suggested":true},{"name":"Tasting Georgia: A Food and Wine Journey in the Caucasus","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Carla Capalbo, 2017","note":"Region-by-region guide to Georgian food and wine with recipes.","url":"","suggested":true},{"name":"Supra: A Feast of Georgian Cooking","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Tiko Tuskadze, 2017","note":"Georgian home recipes from the owner of a London Georgian restaurant.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Walnut","ingredient/walnut"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Vinegar","ingredient/vinegar"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Prunus cerasifera","ingredient/prunus-cerasifera"],["Tkemali","ingredient/tkemali"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Phaseolus","ingredient/phaseolus"],["Juglans regia","ingredient/juglans-regia"],["Khachapuri","ingredient/khachapuri"],["Sulguni","ingredient/sulguni"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Herbs","ingredient/herbs"],["Khmeli suneli","ingredient/khmeli-suneli"],["Paprika","ingredient/paprika"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Caucasian cuisine","cuisine/caucasian-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/40/Georgia%2C_the_Art_of_the_Feast.jpg/500px-Georgia%2C_the_Art_of_the_Feast.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Irma Sharikadze (ირმა შარიქაძე)","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georgia%2C_the_Art_of_the_Feast.jpg"}},"cuisine/fasting-and-abstinence-in-the-catholic-church":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/fasting-and-abstinence-in-the-catholic-church","n":"Catholic diet","c":"#a99fb5","crumb":[["Christian diet","cuisine/christian-dietary-laws"]],"sub":"Religious cuisine or diet","intro":[["The Catholic Church observes the disciplines of fasting and abstinence (from meat) at various times each year. For Catholics, fasting is the reduction of one's intake of food, while abstinence refers to refraining from something that is good, and not inherently sinful, such as meat. The Catholic Church teaches that all people are obliged by God to perform some penance for their sins, and that these acts of penance are both personal and corporeal."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fasting_and_abstinence_in_the_Catholic_Church"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Catholic Culture: Recipes for the Liturgical Year","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"catholicculture.org","note":"Catholic recipe archive tied to feast days and fasting seasons such as Lent.","url":"https://catholicculture.org/culture/liturgicalyear/recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"A Continual Feast: A Cookbook to Celebrate the Joys of Family and Faith throughout the Christian Year","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Evelyn Birge Vitz","note":"Ignatius Press cookbook of dishes for feast days and fasting seasons across the church year.","url":"https://ignatius.com/a-continual-feast-cfep/","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780898703849"}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Christian diet","cuisine/christian-dietary-laws"]]}],"cont":null,"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/24/PlateOfFishLg.jpg/500px-PlateOfFishLg.jpg","w":500,"h":332,"by":"JohnHarvey","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlateOfFishLg.jpg"}},"dish/antipasto":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/antipasto","n":"Antipasto","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["An antipasto is the traditional first course of a formal Italian meal. Usually made of bite-size small portions and presented on a platter from which everyone serves themselves, the purpose of antipasti is to stimulate the appetite. The antipasto is typically followed by the primo piatto."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-antipasto"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antipasto"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Lunch meat","ingredient/lunch-meat"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Manu's Menu","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","u